q BT 65.20 721.50 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (It was past midnight when Don Adrian Cole heard the small sound from his study.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 692.02 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.294 Tw (He had been working late, as he always did -- the house asleep, the city quiet below the hill,) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 671.61 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (only the desk lamp burning. The sound was soft. A child's footsteps, bare on marble.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 642.13 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (He looked up.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 612.65 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.114 Tw (A little girl stood in front of the big portrait on the far wall. She wore a pink nightdress, her dark) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 592.24 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (hair loose around her shoulders. She could not have been more than three years old.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 562.76 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg ("She cries at night," the little girl said, without turning around. "I hear her.") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 533.28 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (Adrian put down his pen. "That's my mother," he said. "She's been dead twenty years.") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 503.80 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.181 Tw (The girl turned then. She had large dark eyes and no fear in them at all. "I know," she said. "She) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 483.39 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (told me where the letter is.") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 453.91 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.124 Tw (Before Adrian could answer, the door flew open. A young woman rushed in -- the new maid,) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 433.50 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (Elena, her face white with panic. She swept the child up into her arms.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 404.02 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg ("I'm sorry, Don," she said, breathless. "She shouldn't be here. She sleepwalks. I'm so sorry--") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 374.54 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg ("Wait." Adrian stood up. "How does she know my mother's face?") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 345.06 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.208 Tw (Elena froze. The child, Lily, looked at him over her mother's shoulder and said, quite calmly,) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 324.65 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg ("Behind her.") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 295.17 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg ("Behind who?" Adrian asked.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 265.69 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg ("Behind your mother," Lily said. "The letter is behind her.") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 236.21 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.311 Tw (Adrian had not touched that portrait in twenty years. It hung where it had always hung -- his) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 215.80 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.449 Tw (mother, painted at forty, her dark hair pinned up, her mouth set in the line he remembered from) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 195.39 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (childhood. The staff dusted it. Nobody moved it.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 165.91 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.098 Tw (He lifted it off the wall himself, his hands shaking in a way they had not shaken in forty years of) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 145.50 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (business.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 116.02 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.841 Tw (Behind it, taped to the back of the frame, was a letter. Yellowed. Sealed with wax that had) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 95.61 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (cracked with age.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 66.13 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.551 Tw (He knew the handwriting before he broke the seal. His mother's hand. He would have known it) Tj ET Q
