q BT 65.20 653.47 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (My dearest son. If you are reading this, I am gone, and the child is old enough to ask questions.) Tj ET Q
BT /F4 12.00 Tf ET
q BT 65.20 623.99 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (His eyes moved down the page. Then stopped.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 594.51 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg ("Protect the child," he read aloud. "She is his.") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 565.03 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg ("Whose child?" Adrian looked up at Elena. "Whose?") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 535.55 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.737 Tw (Elena set Lily down gently. The little girl walked to Adrian and took his hand -- a small warm) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 515.14 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (hand, trusting him completely, as if she had always known he was hers.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 485.66 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg ("Your son's," Elena said. "Lily is your granddaughter.") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 456.18 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.027 Tw (Adrian's son had died at nineteen. A car crash on a wet road, a funeral with a closed coffin, a) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 435.77 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 2.808 Tw (grave Adrian visited every year on the same grey November morning. His son had never) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 415.36 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.444 Tw (married. There had been no wife, no child, no one. The family line had ended in that crash, and) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 394.95 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (Adrian had carried that ending alone for forty-three years.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 365.47 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg ("You are lying," he said, but his voice had no force in it.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 335.99 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.587 Tw ("I married your son in secret," Elena said. "He was nineteen. I was eighteen. We were going to) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 315.58 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (tell you after his birthday. Then the crash came, and I was already carrying Lily.") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 286.10 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.164 Tw (She told it plainly, the way people tell things they have rehearsed for years. She had come to the) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 265.69 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.613 Tw (house to work as a maid because it was the only way to be near the family she could never) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 245.28 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.233 Tw (claim. Her mother -- the old maid -- had known everything, and had hidden the letter behind the) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 224.87 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.293 Tw (portrait the night Adrian's mother died, with instructions to wait until Lily was old enough to) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 204.46 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (find it herself.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 174.98 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.143 Tw ("Then why was she hidden from me?" Adrian asked. His voice broke on the last word. "Why) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 154.57 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (did no one tell me I had a granddaughter?") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 125.09 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (Elena looked at the letter in his hand. "Because someone in this family wanted her gone.") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 95.61 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (The letter named him.) Tj ET Q
